r the other copy's choice actually depends on what I'm deciding, since it's running on a different input, y. The recipe only draws a dependence edge when the other copy computes my function on the same input, so this comes down to whether it counts as the red/blue case. Next I want a prior on fdt(y).\n\nThe inputs differ only in names and the lead text, so the decision function should treat them the same way, which means the other copy likely depends strongly on my choice, with weight rho. Under that dependence, I'm comparing how many years sending versus staying quiet would cost, and the sign of that difference depends on the other copy's sending probability s when it isn't dependent.\n\nI'm working out where the threshold lands: the other copy's sending probability s = 0.5 gives a cutoff at rho above 3/7, and with the inputs differing only in irrelevant details I'd expect rho to be high, so I'm choosing to pass. I also want to note that mutual quiet is the self-consistent fixed point.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm checking whether the other copy's choice actually depends on what I'm deciding, since it's running on a different input, y. The recipe only draws a dependence edge when the other copy computes my function on the same input, so this comes down to whether it counts as the red/blue case. Next I want a prior on fdt(y).\n\nThe inputs differ only in names and the lead text, so the decision function should treat them the same way, which means the other copy likely depends strongly on my choice, with weight rho. Under that dependence, I'm comparing how many years sending versus staying quiet would cost, and the sign of that difference depends on the other copy's sending probability s when it isn't dependent.\n\nI'm working out where the threshold lands: the other copy's sending probability s = 0.5 gives a cutoff at rho above 3/7, and with the inputs differing only in irrelevant details I'd expect rho to be high, so I'm choosing to pass. I also want to note that mutual quiet is the self-consistent fixed point.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9732,"completion_tokens":1251,"total_tokens":10983,"cost":0.063948,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.063948,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.038928,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.02502},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":687,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}